WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Type II is the bread and butter of residential HVAC. This is what you'll use
every day.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Type II recovery requirements depend on system charge size. Systems under 200
lbs: recover to 0 psig. Systems 200 lbs or more: recover to 10 inches Hg vacuum.
These levels apply when using recovery equipment manufactured after November 15,

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
De Minimis Release: The small unavoidable release when connecting or
disconnecting hoses. This is the only legal release.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Know these recovery levels cold for the EPA
608 exam and for every service call.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Under 200 lbs = 0 psig. And — Over 200 lbs = 10 inches Hg
vacuum

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
What recovery level do you need on a system under 200 pounds using post-1993
equipment? Know that cold.

